# Flatness and freeness of the stalk of a module on a geometric fibre

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` of a big fppf site, let `F`
be an `𝒪_X`-module, let `x̄` be a geometric point of `X` and let `ȳ = f ∘ x̄`.  Stacks 0CZS says
that, for `f` locally of finite presentation and `F` of finite presentation and flat at `x` over
`Y`, the following are equivalent:

1. `(F_{ȳ})_{x̄}` is a flat `𝒪_{X_{ȳ}, x̄}`-module,
2. `(F_{ȳ})_{x̄}` is a free `𝒪_{X_{ȳ}, x̄}`-module,
3. `F_{ȳ}` is finite free in an étale neighbourhood of `x̄` in `X_{ȳ}`,
4. `F` is finite free in an étale neighbourhood of `x` in `X`.

This file supplies the geometric fibre stalk and its base ring, the equivalence of (1) and (2)
over it, the identification of (1) with condition (1) of Stacks 05WY at `𝟙 X` over `f`, and the
freeness of the geometric stalk `F_{x̄}` itself that (1) and the standing flatness hypothesis
imply.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.geometricFibreIdeal`: the ideal `𝔪_{ȳ} 𝒪_{X, x̄}` of the étale local
  ring of `X` at `x̄` generated by the image of the maximal ideal of `𝒪_{Y, ȳ}`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.geometricFibreLocalRing`: the ring `𝒪_{X_{ȳ}, x̄}`, as the quotient
  `𝒪_{X, x̄} / 𝔪_{ȳ} 𝒪_{X, x̄}`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.geometricFibreModuleStalk`: the module `(F_{ȳ})_{x̄}`, as the quotient
  `F_{x̄} / 𝔪_{ȳ} F_{x̄}` of the geometric stalk of Stacks 05VQ.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocalRing_geometricFibreLocalRing`: `𝒪_{X_{ȳ}, x̄}` is a local ring.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_geometricFibreModuleStalk_of_free`: **Stacks 0CZS, (2) implies
  (1)**.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_geometricFibreModuleStalk_iff_free`: **Stacks 0CZS, (1) is
  equivalent to (2)**, for a fibre stalk which is a finite module.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.module_finite_geometricFibreModuleStalk`: the fibre stalk of a
  quasi-coherent module of finite type is a finite module.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_geometricFibreModuleStalk_iff_free_of_isFinitePresentation`:
  **Stacks 0CZS, (1) is equivalent to (2)** for a finitely presented module, with no hypothesis
  beyond the source's own.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.etaleLocalRingMap_id` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFlatOverAtGeometricPoint_id_iff`: the canonical homomorphism of
  étale local rings of Stacks 04NG at an identity is the identity, and flatness over the source
  itself is flatness of the geometric stalk.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFibreFlatOverAtGeometricPoint_id_iff`: clause (1) is condition (1)
  of Stacks 05WY for `X ⟶ X ⟶ Y`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.free_geometricModuleStalk_of_flat_geometricFibreModuleStalk`: with
  the source's standing hypothesis that `F` is flat at `x` over `Y`, clause (1) makes the
  geometric stalk `F_{x̄}` a free `𝒪_{X, x̄}`-module.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_geometricFibreModuleStalk_of_free_geometricModuleStalk` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_geometricFibreModuleStalk_iff_free_geometricModuleStalk`: clause
  (1) holds as soon as the geometric stalk `F_{x̄}` is free — with no hypothesis at all — so
  under the source's hypotheses clause (1) *is* freeness of `F_{x̄}`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.free_chartZariskiModuleStalk_of_free_geometricModuleStalk`: freeness
  of the geometric stalk `F_{x̄}` descends across the comparison of Stacks 05VP to freeness of
  the Zariski stalk `(φ^* F)_u` of the chart restriction, at any rank.  This is the first step
  of the source's `(1) ⟹ (4)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.free_geometricModuleStalk_of_free_chartZariskiModuleStalk` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.free_geometricModuleStalk_iff_free_chartZariskiModuleStalk`: the
  converse of that descent, and the resulting equivalence — the first step of the source's
  `(4) ⟹ (1)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_chartOpen_over_iso_free_of_flat_geometricFibreModuleStalk`:
  **Stacks 0CZS, clause (4)**, in the reading the source's own proof produces — `F` becomes
  finite free on a Zariski open neighbourhood of `u` in an étale scheme chart `(U, u)` of `x̄`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.free_chartZariskiModuleStalk_of_over_iso_free`: such a
  trivialization makes the Zariski stalk `(φ^* F)_u` free, which is the inverse of the
  Stacks 0B8J step clause (4) uses.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_geometricFibreModuleStalk_of_exists_chartOpen_over_iso_free`:
  **Stacks 0CZS, clause (4) implies clause (1)**, needing only quasi-coherence of `F`, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_chartOpen_over_iso_free_iff_flat_geometricFibreModuleStalk`:
  **Stacks 0CZS, clause (1) if and only if clause (4)**.

Clause (3) of Stacks 0CZS is not stated here; see the implementation notes.

## Implementation notes

The fibre of a morphism of algebraic spaces over a point of the target is not constructed in
this library — `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fiberOverField` is the fibre over a *field-valued* point
and lives over that point's field — so `𝒪_{X_{ȳ}, x̄}` and `(F_{ȳ})_{x̄}` cannot be formed as the
étale local ring and the geometric stalk of an algebraic space `X_{ȳ}`.  They are formed instead
in the quotient form

```
𝒪_{X_{ȳ}, x̄} = 𝒪_{X, x̄} / 𝔪_{ȳ} 𝒪_{X, x̄},    (F_{ȳ})_{x̄} = F_{x̄} / 𝔪_{ȳ} F_{x̄},
```

which is how the source's own proof reads clause (1): it applies Stacks 05WY to
`id : X ⟶ X` over `Y`, and condition (1) of that lemma is exactly flatness of this quotient
module over this quotient ring.  Stacks 05WY is available, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_flatQuotSMul_chart_iff_isFibreFlatOverAtGeometricPoint` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/FibreFlatnessGeometricPoint.lean`, and its condition (1)
is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFibreFlatOverAtGeometricPoint`; the quotients below are that
condition's constituents at `𝟙 X` over `f`, written out, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFibreFlatOverAtGeometricPoint_id_iff` proves that they are.  That
identification rests on `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.etaleLocalRingMap_id`: the canonical map of
Stacks 04NG is defined by a choice from a unique-existence statement, so the identity case is
obtained from `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.eq_etaleLocalRingMap` by checking the germ condition
against the cocone defining the stalk colimit, the point `geometricPointMap (𝟙 X) x̄ = x̄` being
a definitional equality.  The identification of the quotient with the étale local ring of an
actual geometric fibre `X_{ȳ}` is not claimed.  The ideal is the image of the maximal ideal of
`𝒪_{Y, ȳ}` along the canonical map of étale local rings of Stacks 04NG,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.etaleLocalRingMap`, and the module structure of the quotient module
over the quotient ring is Mathlib's instance for `M ⧸ I • ⊤` over `R ⧸ I`, so no scalar
restriction is needed.

The étale local rings are local by Stacks 08AH
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocalRing_etaleLocalRing`), which needs the algebraicity hypothesis
and so is installed locally rather than found by instance search.  The ideal `𝔪_{ȳ} 𝒪_{X, x̄}` is
proper because the canonical map of étale local rings is local
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocalHom_etaleLocalRingMap`), whence the quotient is a nontrivial
quotient of a local ring and so local itself.

The equivalence of (1) and (2) assumes neither that `F` is flat at `x` over `Y` nor that `f` is
locally of finite presentation: both clauses are conditions on the fibre stalk alone, and the
implications hold without those hypotheses.  Dropping them is a generalisation of the source.

What the source *does* use is that the fibre stalk is a finite module over the fibre local ring,
which it gets from finite presentation of `F`.  That route is taken here: the geometric stalk of
a quasi-coherent module of finite type is a finite module over the étale local ring
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.module_finite_geometricModuleStalk`), and finiteness descends to the
quotient by `𝔪_{ȳ}` and then along the surjection onto the quotient ring.  A finitely presented
sheaf of modules on a site is quasi-coherent and of finite type, so
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_geometricFibreModuleStalk_iff_free_of_isFinitePresentation` needs
nothing beyond the source's hypotheses; the version taking finiteness of the fibre stalk as the
hypothesis `hfin` is kept because it holds for any module with a finite fibre stalk and in any
module universe, whereas the stalk-finiteness input is available only when the module sections
live in the universe of the schemes.  Given finiteness, (1) implies (2) is Stacks 00NZ,
`Module.free_of_flat_of_isLocalRing`, and the converse is `Module.Flat.of_free`.

Beyond the equivalence of (1) and (2), clause (1) together with the source's standing
hypothesis makes the geometric stalk `F_{x̄}` itself a free `𝒪_{X, x̄}`-module.  This is the
source's `(1) ⟹ (4)` short of its last step, and it is obtained by instantiating Stacks 05X0
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFlatOverAtGeometricPoint_and_isFibreFlat_iff`) at `𝟙 X` over `f`:
its hypothesis (1) becomes the standing flatness together with clause (1), and its conclusion
(2) delivers flatness over `𝒪_{X, x̄}`, whence freeness since the stalk is finite over a local
ring.  Stacks 05X0 assumes a nonzero stalk; a zero stalk is free, so the two cases are split.
Finite presentation of `F` enters there in the chartwise form
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFinitePresentationOnCharts`, which is the reading Stacks 05X0 uses.

Clauses (3) and (4) speak of finite freeness in an étale neighbourhood, of `X_{ȳ}` and of `X`
respectively.  Clause (3) needs the geometric fibre `X_{ȳ}` as an algebraic space and so is not
statable.  Clause (4) is stated and proved from clause (1),
as `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_chartOpen_over_iso_free_of_flat_geometricFibreModuleStalk`.

The source reads clause (4) through an étale scheme chart: it chooses `φ : (U, u) → (X, x̄)` with
`U` a scheme and asserts that `φ^* F` is finite free near `u`.  The first step is therefore to
descend freeness of `F_{x̄}` over `𝒪_{X, x̄}` to freeness of the Zariski stalk `(φ^* F)_u` over
`𝒪_{U, u}`, and that is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.free_chartZariskiModuleStalk_of_free_geometricModuleStalk` below.  Its
three inputs are all available: the comparison of Stacks 05VP presents `F_{x̄}` as the base change
of `(φ^* F)_u` along the faithfully flat `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isIso_chartStalkTensorComparison` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.faithfullyFlat_chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing`), the chart stalk is
finitely presented over the local ring of the chart
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.finitePresentation_chartZariskiModuleStalk`), and descent of flatness
along a faithfully flat base change is Mathlib's `Module.Flat.of_flat_tensorProduct`.  That last
lemma — for a faithfully flat `C → C'` and a `C`-module `N`, flatness of `C' ⊗_C N` over `C'`
implies flatness of `N` over `C` — is in `Mathlib/RingTheory/Flat/FaithfullyFlat/Basic.lean` and
is used in a dozen places in this library.  Flatness and freeness agree for the chart
stalk because it is finitely presented over the local ring `𝒪_{U, u}`.

The last step is the scheme-level Stacks 0B8J, which turns freeness of the stalk of a finitely
presented module on a topological space into freeness on an open neighbourhood.  It is used
through `Stacks.StalkFiniteType.exists_over_iso_free_of_stalk_basis`, the form of 0B8J whose
hypothesis is a basis over the `CommRingCat`-valued local ring `𝒪_{U, u}` rather than over the
`RingCat`-valued stalk of `𝒪_U ⋙ forget₂` that
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_iso_free_over_of_stalk_iso_free` asks for; the two base rings are
different filtered colimits and `Stacks.StalkFiniteType.basisRingCatStalk` is the transport
between them.  Two further identifications one might expect are not needed at all:

* no comparison between the stalk of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictToChart` and the stalk of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRestrictionPresheafOfModules` has to be made, because the
  latter *is* `(restrictToChart ...).val` by definition and 0B8J reads the stalk of `M.val`
  — so the sheafification never has to be unwound; and
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFinitePresentation_restrictToChart_iff` is not the bridge to the
  Zariski-site finite presentation 0B8J wants, because no bridge is needed:
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFinitePresentationOnCharts` is by definition the statement that
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictToChart` is of finite presentation at every chart
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartModule` being an abbreviation for it), which is that
  hypothesis on the nose.

The open neighbourhood of `u` in `U` which 0B8J produces is an étale neighbourhood of `x̄` in
`X`, by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartOpenNeighborhood`; so the conclusion below, a Zariski
open of an étale scheme chart on which the chart restriction becomes finite free, is clause (4).
The declaration below does not *claim* the identification of `(φ^* F)|_W`, a module on the slice
of the Zariski site of `U` at `W`, with the chart restriction of `F` to `W` read on the Zariski
site of `W` itself; but that identification is available.  It is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.nonempty_over_restrictToChart_chartOpenNeighborhood` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ChartOpenRestrictionOver.lean`, on quasi-coherence of `F`
alone, and what makes it expressible is that the chart scheme of the chart `W` cuts out *is* the
open subscheme `W` and the restricted structure sheaf *is* its structure sheaf, both by `rfl`.

The predicate of clause (4) exists:
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.etaleFiniteFreeLocus` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/EtaleFreeLocus.lean` is the locus of points of `|X|` at
which `F` is finite free in an étale neighbourhood, with the neighbourhood an étale morphism of
algebraic spaces and the freeness read on the small étale site.  That reading is not the one the
source's proof produces — the source produces freeness on the *Zariski* site of a scheme chart —
so passing between them is a further comparison.  The implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/EtaleFreeLocus.lean` enumerate **three** inputs for the
base-change clause of Stacks 0CZT, this comparison being the third.

That third input is complete in the direction clause (4) *produces* — Zariski to small étale.
Its two ingredients are
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.nonempty_over_restrictToChart_chartOpenNeighborhood` (above) and, in
the namespace `AlgebraicGeometry`,
`Space.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_over_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_chartSchemeModule` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/FiniteLocallyFreeRankChartScheme.lean`, Stacks 03DX (2)
with
a rank.  The first input, the base-change invariance of clause (1), is proved as well:
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_geometricFibreModuleStalk_modulePullback_iff` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/GeometricFibreStalkBaseChange.lean`.  It does not depend
on condition (2) of Stacks 05WY: the invariance follows directly, at the étale local rings,
from the cartesian input of
Stacks 05VW (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.cartesian_etaleStalk_tensor_flat`) — because at the
*fibre* the comparison becomes a base change along a homomorphism out of a field, so the fibre
local ring upstairs is faithfully flat over the one downstairs without any flatness of the base
change.  What separates clause (4) from the base-change clause of Stacks 0CZT is the
assembly of the two ends of the transport; see the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/EtaleFreeLocus.lean`.

**The converse direction `(4) ⟹ (1)` is proved below, in three steps, and needs none of the
source's hypotheses except quasi-coherence of `F`.**  The chain is
`trivialization on a Zariski open ⟹ (φ^* F)_u free ⟹ F_{x̄} free ⟹ clause (1)`.

The last two links are base changes of a free module along a ring homomorphism
(`Algebra.TensorProduct.instFree`): along the comparison of Stacks 05VP for
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.free_geometricModuleStalk_of_free_chartZariskiModuleStalk`, which is
where quasi-coherence is used and where the descending direction — but not this one — needs
faithful flatness; and along `𝒪_{X, x̄} → 𝒪_{X, x̄} / 𝔪_{ȳ} 𝒪_{X, x̄}`, through
`TensorProduct.quotTensorEquivQuotSMul`, for
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_geometricFibreModuleStalk_of_free_geometricModuleStalk`.

The first link, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.free_chartZariskiModuleStalk_of_over_iso_free`, is the
inverse of the Stacks 0B8J step clause (4) uses, and it is
`LocallyFreeRank.Trivialization.stalk_linearEquiv_finsupp` of
`StacksFrontier/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/LocallyFreeRank.lean` after two identifications,
both of which hold on the nose: the Zariski ring sheaf of the chart scheme is the
`LocallyFreeRank.toRingSheaf` of its sheaf of commutative rings, and the slice of the chart's
Zariski site at `W` carries the same sheaf of modules as the open subspace `W`
(`LocallyFreeRank.restrictModIsoOver`, an `Iso.refl`).  The free module crosses the comparison
by `SheafOfModules.mapFreeIso`, the comparison being an equivalence and so preserving the unit
and coproducts, and `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartZariskiModuleStalkStalkEquiv` identifies the
stalk the general form computes with the Zariski stalk of Stacks 05VP.

The module universe of the geometric stalk is independent of the universe of the schemes, as in
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.geometricModuleStalk`, and is kept so below.

